<div class="page">

  <div class="header">
    <div class="arrow-line left"></div>
    <h1><span class="script">Social</span><span class="block">DISTANCING</span></h1>
    <div class="arrow-line right"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="main-section">
    <div class="col-left">
      <div class="icon-circle">&#8596;</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">WHAT IS SOCIAL<br>DISTANCING?</h2>
      <p class="section-text">
        Social distancing, also called physical distancing, is a form of
        <strong>non-pharmaceutical intervention</strong>, which downtrends the spread
        of contagious diseases simply by <strong>keeping people "apart" from each other.</strong>
      </p>

      <div class="block-gap">
        <div class="icon-circle">&#33;</div>
        <h2 class="section-title">WHY IS SOCIAL<br>DISTANCING IMPORTANT?</h2>
        <p class="section-text">
          It <strong>prevents contact between infected and uninfected individuals</strong>,
          resulting in reduced disease transmission and less deaths from fatal diseases.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-right">
      <div class="practices-title">
        <div class="icon-circle">&#10003;</div>
        <h2>BEST PRACTICES FOR<br>SOCIAL DISTANCING</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="practice-item">
        <div class="practice-icon">&#8962;</div>
        <div class="practice-text">
          <strong>Self/Home Quarantine: Stay home.</strong> Only go out if it's very essential,
          that too with protection (gloves, masks, sanitizers)
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="practice-item">
        <div class="practice-icon">&#128101;</div>
        <div class="practice-text">
          <strong>Avoid public gatherings</strong> as much as possible
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="practice-item">
        <div class="practice-icon">&#127978;</div>
        <div class="practice-text">
          Keep spots susceptible to mass gatherings like <strong>parks, malls, food courts, restaurants
          and schools closed.</strong> Restaurants can be instructed to follow a "Takeaway" only system
          until the situation relaxes
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="practice-item">
        <div class="practice-icon">&#128207;</div>
        <div class="practice-text">
          Maintain a distance of <strong>at least 1 - 2 meters (3 to 6 feet)</strong> from other individuals
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="practice-item">
        <div class="practice-icon">&#129309;</div>
        <div class="practice-text">
          <strong>Avoid shaking hands</strong> and embracing one another
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="bottom-section">
    <div class="bottom-header">
      <div class="icon-circle">&#128200;</div>
      <h2>SOCIAL DISTANCING IN THE TIME<br>OF COVID-19: FLATTENING THE CURVE</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="bottom-text">
      For a disease like COVID-19, which spreads through air droplets from sneezing and coughing,
      scientists have claimed that <strong>social distancing might "flatten the curve".</strong>
    </p>
    <p class="bottom-text">
      This means that if proper social distancing protocols are followed, the spread of the disease
      will <strong>slow down and relieve health care professionals and medical centers</strong> of the
      burden of providing aid to hundreds of patients at a time, which is not feasible.
    </p>
  </div>

